WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.267
-Hi. I'm Jimmy Fallon,

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:04.734
one of the few TV personalities
who's still employed.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:08.767
Tucker Carlson, Don Lemon --
what's the --

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:10.968
what the hell's
going on out there?

00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:13.200
Everyone's talking about this.
Today, Fox News announced

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.200
that they are parting ways
with Tucker Carlson.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:23.801
Some people aren't sure
what led to his exit,

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:26.701
but Fox said that they can think
of almost a billion reasons why.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:28.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.634
Yep, Tucker Carlson is out.

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:32.133
When he heard,
Vladimir Putin was like,

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.701
[ Russian accent ]
"Damn, we need a new P.R. guy."

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:36.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:37.801
[ Normal voice ]
It's easy to make jokes

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.601
about Tucker being gone,
but now who's gonna tell me

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:41.601
which M&amp;M is most woke?
You know?

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:44.300
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.300
Fox knows their viewers
are gonna miss Tucker,

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.934
so until they find
a replacement,

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.667
his show will be hosted
by a golf shirt

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:50.901
with the collars popped.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:54.901
Yeah, it was a big day
in the cable-news world

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.400
because just minutes after
the Tucker story broke,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.734
Don Lemon announced
that he was fired by CNN.

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:01.901
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:03.968
When he found out that he
no longer worked at CNN,

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.834
Lemon was like...

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:10.200
"Whoo-hoo!
Later, suckers! Ha ha!"

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.167
Meanwhile, some more
big news at CNN.

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:16.834
The network announced that
Gayle King and Charles Barkley

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:20.300
will host a new weekly
show called "King Charles."

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:24.701
[ Questlove laughing ]

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.334
That's not a joke.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:28.133
Gayle King...
-Right.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.100
-...and Charles Barkley.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.133
So it's called "King Charles."
-Charles.

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:33.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:35.267
-Well, I guess it's better

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.968
than if some other celebrities
teamed up for a show.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:39.501
For instance,
if Jean-Claude Van Damme

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:41.100
teamed up with Daniel Craig,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.834
you would get Damme, Daniel!

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:46.934
I might've watched that.
-Yeah. Come on.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.701
The new Van.
-You know.

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:53.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.467
Let me give you
another example.

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:57.868
If you teamed up with Kid Rock,
Emma Stone, and NeNe Leakes,

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.400
you get Kid Ne Stone.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.434
You know, and you go...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:05.200
If you teamed up Susan Boyle,
Christopher Nolan,

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.934
and Leonardo DiCaprio, you get
Sus, No Cap.

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:10.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.701
If you teamed up Joe Pesci
and (Not) Coco Gauff,

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.200
you get,
Sorry, We Don't Have Coco.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:18.334
Is Pesci Okay?

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:22.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:24.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:27.534
I would watch
all of these shows.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.400
I love Gayle and Charles.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.767
Some big news from Washington.

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:32.868
Tomorrow, President Biden
is expected to announce

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:34.934
his re-election campaign.

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:37.734
Biden said, "I really want
four more years as president

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:38.934
and in general."

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:44.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:49.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:51.334
Tomorrow's announcement
is expected to be met

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:54.100
with the world's slowest clap
from Kamala Harris.

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:56.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.067
"Four more years."

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:01.133
Yeah, Biden said he wants four
more years to get the job done.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:03.701
And Americans were like,
"We've already given you 50.

00:03:03.701 --> 00:03:06.534
Get it done."
Come on. Gosh.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:07.634
I actually read that
Biden plans

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:09.033
to kick off
his re-election campaign

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:11.601
with a "low-key"
video announcement.

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:12.801
We actually got
a preview of it,

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:15.868
and I'm not sure
how low-key it is.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.300
Take a look at this.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.601
-What's up, America?!

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.767
You ready to go insane
for another Biden campaign?!

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.033
Hyah!

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:23.567
I know what you're thinking.
He's older than Lincoln.

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:24.734
[ Train whistle blows ]

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:27.767
But his old ass
is gonna get bills passed!

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:30.868
Joe's got the mojo,
and America needs mo' Joe!

00:03:30.868 --> 00:03:33.767
He's ready to fight even though
he can't drive at night!

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:36.300
He'll debate in all 50 states!
-Master debater!

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.667
-No ifs, ands, or buts!

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:39.367
He'll kick inflation
in the nuts!

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:40.667
-Aah!
-And you know he's gonna

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:42.701
tax the rich, bitch!

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:46.133
So chip in some cash
or he'll spank dat ass!

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:47.968
Joe's ready to run!
Not literally.

00:03:47.968 --> 00:03:49.934
So strap in
for some [bleep] fun.

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:52.200
Now get out the vote
for the 80-year-old GOAT!

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.734
[ Goat screams ]
Whoo!

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.067
-That's not low-key.

00:03:56.067 --> 00:04:01.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
That is not low-key at all!

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:02.667
-[ Laughing ]

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:05.334
-Some business news.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.701
Bed, Bath &amp; Beyond
has filed for bankruptcy

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:10.734
and will close permanently
in the next few months.

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:12.501
It's crazy.
A business crashed and burn

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:15.334
without being run by Elon Musk.
Isn't that unbelievable?

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:16.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:18.601
Right now, Kmart is like,
"Whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:19.901
You still think
you're better than us,

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:22.234
Bed, Bath &amp; Beyond?
[ Clicks tongue ]

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.300
Let us know how 'beyond' is,
okay?"

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:29.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:30.634
You guys see this?

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.400
On Saturday night,
during a show at Disneyland,

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.133
a 45-foot-tall animatronic
dragon caught on fire.

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:37.667
Take a look at this.
It's real.

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:43.701
♪♪

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:45.133
-Your attention, please.

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:47.734
Due to unforeseen circumstances,

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:51.434
this performance of Fantasmic
cannot continue.

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:53.033
Thank you.
-Ohh!

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.400
-Whoa!

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:58.701
-Of course, it's Disneyland,
so they offer to sell people

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:00.567
a photo of themselves
running for their lives.

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:03.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:05.534
"50 bucks."

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:06.801
Well, this is going viral.

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:08.267
A movie theater
in Alaska recently

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:12.601
had an unexpected visitor.
Check this out.

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:14.734
-Oh, my gosh, bro.

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:21.167
[ Laughs ]

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:23.267
-It's a moose.

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:25.501
Yeah. Everyone at the theater
got to play a fun game of,

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:27.400
"Is that or is
that not a milk dud?"

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.434
Very interesting.

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:32.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:35.234
-"Not!"
-Finally...

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:38.334
Finally, a new poll found
that nearly 40% feel exhaustion

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:41.601
over the idea of a Biden-Trump
rematch in 2024.

00:05:41.601 --> 00:05:42.767
Very interesting poll.

00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:44.567
Check out some
of the other data they released.

00:05:44.567 --> 00:05:47.334
First up, when asked,
"Who will you vote for in 2024?"

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:50.167
5% said Trump, 5% said Biden,

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:53.000
90% said, "Whoever can score me
Taylor Swift tickets."

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.234 --> 00:06:01.234
"I got to see Eras.
I got to see Eras."

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:03.300
-Up next, when asked,
"Are you excited about voting?"

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.934
70% said no.
30% said, "Only if we're talking

00:06:06.934 --> 00:06:09.100
about 'The Masked Singer.'"
Then you go...

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:12.000
"Who's the octopus?"

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.868
Next up, when asked,
"Do you think Nikki Haley,

00:06:13.868 --> 00:06:17.200
Marianne Williamson, or
Asa Hutchinson have a chance?"

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:20.000
99% said, "Lol, no."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.133
1% said, "I don't know
who any of these people are,

00:06:22.133 --> 00:06:24.501
And I'm Asa Hutchinson."
-Wow.

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:29.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:30.767
-Up next, when asked
"Who's the candidate

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:32.467
with the most impressive
résumé?"

00:06:32.467 --> 00:06:35.300
15% said Biden,
10% said Trump,

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.767
75% said George Santos.

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:40.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:40.801 --> 00:06:42.000
It's a great résumé.
-Very impressive.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.067
-Great résumé.
Here's another one.

00:06:44.067 --> 00:06:45.734
When asked, "Where do you get
your news about

00:06:45.734 --> 00:06:47.801
the upcoming election?"
40% said Google,

00:06:47.801 --> 00:06:51.767
40% said TikTok,
19% said Facebook.

00:06:51.767 --> 00:06:53.634
Joe Biden said,
"The town crier."

00:06:53.634 --> 00:06:55.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:55.701 --> 00:06:57.534
"Hear ye, hear ye!"

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:58.901
-Ding ding, ding ding!

00:06:58.901 --> 00:07:00.300
[ Applause ]

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:03.300
[ Drumming ]

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:05.167
Up next, when asked, "What
should the president

00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:06.300
be focused on right now?"

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.467
40% said
reversing climate change,

00:07:08.467 --> 00:07:10.567
40% said
fixing the economy,

00:07:10.567 --> 00:07:12.567
and 40% said
improving our students'

00:07:12.567 --> 00:07:13.701
math and reading scores.

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:19.467
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:07:19.467 --> 00:07:21.767
And finally, when asked,
"Who is the strongest team

00:07:21.767 --> 00:07:25.467
going into the 2024 election?"
20% said Biden-Harris,

00:07:25.467 --> 00:07:27.267
10% said Trump-DeSantis,

00:07:27.267 --> 00:07:29.801
70% said Michelle Obama/
Michelle Obama.

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:31.434
We have --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:33.067
We have a great show.

00:07:33.067 --> 00:07:35.000
Give it up for The Roots,
ladies and gentlemen!

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.000
♪♪

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.834
-♪ Uh-huh ♪

00:07:38.834 --> 00:07:42.334
♪ Once again ♪

00:07:42.334 --> 00:07:44.234
♪ Ladies and gentlemen ♪

00:07:44.234 --> 00:07:48.434
♪♪

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:51.167
-I had a --
I had a very fun weekend.

00:07:51.167 --> 00:07:52.901
-Looked like it.
-Yeah, I went to --

00:07:52.901 --> 00:07:55.634
You saw on the socials?
I went to Vegas.

00:07:55.634 --> 00:07:57.267
I flew to Vegas
because Justin Timberlake

00:07:57.267 --> 00:07:59.767
has a charity golf tournament.

00:07:59.767 --> 00:08:01.834
And I don't really get
to play that much.

00:08:01.834 --> 00:08:04.300
I play it once a year
for this tournament.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:06.133
-Yeah, that's it.
You got a job.

00:08:06.133 --> 00:08:07.801
-Yeah, I work.
Yeah, I love it.

00:08:07.801 --> 00:08:10.133
Yeah. But I went out there.
I had so much fun.

00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:13.167
I was playing with --
Strahan was there,

00:08:13.167 --> 00:08:16.000
but we had JJ Watt was there.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:18.133
Michelle Wie.
Travis Kelce was fun.

00:08:18.133 --> 00:08:21.701
-Oh, he is so fun.
-Kelce did karaoke.

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:22.934
We just got on stage
with the band,

00:08:22.934 --> 00:08:24.634
and he sang AC/DC
"Back in Black."

00:08:24.634 --> 00:08:26.667
It was one of the best things
I've ever seen

00:08:26.667 --> 00:08:28.400
in my entire life.
It was awesome.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.267
I golfed with Justin Timberlake
was my partner. Here we are.

00:08:31.267 --> 00:08:35.467
We wore magnetic belt buckles
one day and that was hard.

00:08:35.467 --> 00:08:36.601
-Look out!

00:08:36.601 --> 00:08:38.868
-That was interesting.
That was hard.

00:08:38.868 --> 00:08:41.434
Anyway, it was fun.
I want to thank everyone.

00:08:41.434 --> 00:08:45.300
Of course, there's only
one winner, and, uh...

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.167
-Oh! Snap!

00:08:48.167 --> 00:08:50.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:50.467 --> 00:08:53.167
Dang!

00:08:53.167 --> 00:08:54.601
Winner!

00:08:54.601 --> 00:08:57.767
Justin Timberlake and I
won the tournament.

00:08:57.767 --> 00:09:01.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:01.434 --> 00:09:03.567
Thank you to 8AM Golf!

00:09:03.567 --> 00:09:05.434
8AM Golf.
And thank you to the win.

00:09:05.434 --> 00:09:08.133
Thank you, Justin.
I'm happy to just be nominated.

00:09:08.133 --> 00:09:10.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:10.667 --> 00:09:12.567
What a show we have
for you tonight.

00:09:12.567 --> 00:09:14.734
She stars in the new movie
"Fool's Paradise,"

00:09:14.734 --> 00:09:17.234
which opens in theaters
May 12th.

00:09:17.234 --> 00:09:19.033
Kate Beckinsale is here tonight!

00:09:19.033 --> 00:09:21.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:21.133 --> 00:09:23.367
Love Kate Beckinsale.

00:09:23.367 --> 00:09:25.534
You know him from "The Office."

00:09:25.534 --> 00:09:29.834
His new book, "Soul Boom: Why We
Need a Spiritual Revolution,"

00:09:29.834 --> 00:09:32.133
it comes out tomorrow, and you
can see him in the series

00:09:32.133 --> 00:09:35.734
"Rainn Wilson and the Geography
of Bliss," on Peacock.

00:09:35.734 --> 00:09:37.467
Rainn Wilson is joining us
tonight!

00:09:37.467 --> 00:09:43.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:43.167 --> 00:09:45.868
And we got great music tonight!
Oh, my gosh.

00:09:45.868 --> 00:09:48.267
One of my favorites.
Romeo Santos.

00:09:48.267 --> 00:09:51.567
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:51.567 --> 00:09:52.767
-We'll be talking to him,

00:09:52.767 --> 00:09:54.834
and he's going to perform later
in the show.

00:09:54.834 --> 00:09:57.300
Stick around. We'll be
right back with Kate Beckinsale,

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.667
ladies and gentlemen.

